built into the caves of Crimea's  balaclava Bay lies a cold war submarine  bunker the Russians started building it  in 1957 it took four years to complete  and was designed to take a direct atomic  strike after a period of decay the  Russians gifted it to the Western  leaning Ukrainians who turned it into  the Cold War Museum Russia is now in  control of Crimea for the time being at  least the base is still a museum I  dropped in for an unexpected incognito  visit obviously very secret base and the  motto is don't say everything you know  and always know what you say in fact the  place was so secretive workers relatives  were barely able to visit paperwork and  thick walls got in the way the whole  base could be hermetically sealed with  these doors and people could stay inside  in the case of a nuclear attack for 3  years Russia has always had a naval base  in Crimea called the Black Sea Fleet  even when it was under Ukrainian control  now Crimea is under Russian control it's  getting bigger with all the talk that  the US and Russia are entering a new  Cold War visiting the Cold War Museum  was more than a little daunting after  the annexation the whole base was  transferred to Russia's Black Sea Fleet  the question now is will it remain a  museum or something else
 

